&lt;style&gt;
	@import url(&#39;https://free-the-people.us/css/global.css&#39;);
    @import url(&#39;https://free-the-people.us/css/post.css&#39;);
    @import url(&#39;https://free-the-people.us/css/newsletter.css&#39;);
&lt;/style&gt;


&lt;section&gt;
    &lt;p class=&quot;tangerine&quot; style=&quot;text-align:center;font-size:4em;padding:1.2rem 0px;&quot;&gt;Impeach. Convict. Remove.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Recap of this week in the revolution: Republicans losing in battleground races. Trump wants Russian oil. Trump sabotages Ukrainian war effort and U.S. tries to dismantle ICC and Trump regime raids Rep. Omar&amp;#39;s home.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-good&quot;&gt;
	&lt;h4&gt;The good...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Republicans realize they are losing in many battleground races, shift campaign spending to areas they think they still have a shot &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/midterms-republicans-democrats-senate-house-cdd95df350c648d19e60cb3ecea42138&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/zxKZVULEqg-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Money and calculator&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/zxKZVULEqg-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;640&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/zxKZVULEqg-200.webp 200w, /images/zxKZVULEqg-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;Image by &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com/users/mohamed_hassan-5229782/?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=10005701&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Mohamed Hassan&lt;/a&gt; from &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com//?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=10005701&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Pixabay&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Republicans are pulling money out of campaigns to support Republicans in key battleground races and shifting it instead to protecting candidates in races that were once believed to be guaranteed wins for their party. This shifting focus shows that the Republican Party knows that they are losing ground anywhere a strong Democratic Party candidate is challenging them, and that even the races they thought they couldn&#39;t lose are suddenly vulnerable to an upset.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;That doesn&#39;t mean that Democrats will necessarily win in the midterms, and Republicans are still ready and able to shovel hundreds of millions of dollars into campaign spending in the final weeks before the midterms...far more than the Democrats can hope to come up with. While Donny 2-Dolls&#39; stunning unpopularity has done significant damage to his party overall, we can&#39;t ignore the influence money has in swaying public opinion. &lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;blockquote&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;Will the unprecedented tsunami of Republican money defeat the massive Democratic advantage in candidates, policies, and political climate?&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;figcaption class=&quot;blockquote-footer&quot;&gt;Senator Chuck Schumer (D-NY)&lt;/figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/blockquote&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
