&lt;section&gt;
    &lt;p class=&quot;tangerine&quot; style=&quot;text-align:center;font-size:4em;padding:1.2rem 0px;&quot;&gt;Impeach. Convict. Remove.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Recap of this week in the revolution: ABC sues FCC over censorship. Hegseth uses military schools to promote propaganda lies. National debt hits new high and Trump plans military invasion of Latin America.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-good&quot;&gt;
	&lt;h4&gt;The good...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        ABC suing FCC for politically-motivated censorship/free speech violations &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/abc-says-fcc-waging-a-retaliatory-campaign-violating-free-speech-rights&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/eCc58wgzaa-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;ABC Logo&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/eCc58wgzaa-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;801&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/eCc58wgzaa-200.webp 200w, /images/eCc58wgzaa-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;The FCC has threatened to strip local ABC stations of their broadcast licenses because the Trump regime doesn&#39;t like some of the content broadcast by Disney-owned ABC stations, especially commentary on the daytime talk show &lt;i&gt;The View.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;The purpose of the licenses issued to broadcasters is to ensure that they use the public airways they control in the public interest. Traditionally, that has been understood to mean that these broadcasters were serving their local communities by sharing information about weather, sports, and news.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Shows like &lt;i&gt;The View&lt;/i&gt; provide commentary on current events that is understood to be protected by the First Amendment right to free speech, and is perfectly acceptable under FCC regulations. It&#39;s worth noting that similar opinion-sharing shows that support the current regime are not being threatened with loss of their licenses.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.pbs.org/newshour/show/abc-says-fcc-waging-a-retaliatory-campaign-violating-free-speech-rights&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(PBS) ABC Says FCC waging a retaliatory campaign violating free speech rights&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-bad&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The bad...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Hegseth wants to use schools on military bases to promote propaganda &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/defense-department-school-classical-hegseth-c29537087c0dbf3271cf293a9b17053f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/O5Ad30jP1m-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;The Golden Thread&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/O5Ad30jP1m-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;1058&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/O5Ad30jP1m-200.webp 200w, /images/O5Ad30jP1m-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;The Golden Thread&lt;/i&gt; book cover.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;Pete Hegseth wants to promote his Christian Nationalist lies in public schools on U.S. military bases. A new western civilization course is being offered based on a curriculum developed by a Christian school in Michigan that pushes patriotic notions giving students the false impression that Christianity and western civilization are under attack by Islam, among other threats.&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;The program claims to offer a classical education, but instead focuses on delivering a biased view of world history, putting the Christian faith and western ideals at the center of the story and downplaying the contributions of other religions and cultures around the world.&lt;/p&gt;
            &lt;p&gt;This new curriculum is in line with the Trump regime&#39;s revisionist history that wants to hide the true but unflattering parts of American history from students and push the false belief that the existence of differing viewpoints or religions represents a threat to the very existence of America and even God, and that students have to oppose those differences of opinion in order to protect their own heritage.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
