&lt;section&gt;
    &lt;p class=&quot;tangerine&quot; style=&quot;text-align:center;font-size:4em;padding:1.2rem 0px;&quot;&gt;Impeach. Convict. Remove.&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;Recap of this week in the revolution: Anti-Weaponization Fund formally canceled and Pirro admits no evidence of vandalism in Reflecting Pool case. Trump regime withdraws deportation protections for military families. ICE will withhold footage from new body cameras unless it shows agents in a favorable light.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-good&quot;&gt;
	&lt;h4&gt;The good...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Blanche agrees to kill $1.8 billion January 6 compensation fund in exchange for getting his nomination for Attorney General through committee &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/senate-blanche-trump-justice-fund-a38decfc7f20e4f73a181914d53111da&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/-usngkcRUs-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Images from January 6, 2021, insurrection&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/-usngkcRUs-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;800&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/-usngkcRUs-200.webp 200w, /images/-usngkcRUs-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Images from January 6, 2021, insurrection, including the noose that was raised with the intention of hanging Vice President Mike Pence.&lt;/b&gt; Image by &lt;a href=&quot;https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Aca1291&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Aca1291&lt;/a&gt; from &lt;a href=&quot;https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2021_United_States_Capitol_attack_collage.jpg&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Wikimedia Commons.&lt;/a&gt; Licensed under the &lt;a href=&quot;https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0 International license&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;In January of this year, Donny 2-Dolls filed a lawsuit against his own Department of Treasury alleging the IRS leaked his 2019-2020 tax returns to the press. The DOJ settled the case out of court and, instead of pursuing the case, agreed to create a $1.8 billion fund to provide payments to January 6 insurrectionists who claimed they were unfairly prosecuted. In addition, the settlement included a provision that the Trump family and businesses could never be audited by the IRS for past or future inquiries.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Todd Blanche was nominated to replace Pam Bondi as Attorney General of the United States, but his confirmation has been held up because not all Republicans have been willing to support his nomination. This week, the last two Republican holdouts agreed to support Blanche&#39;s nomination in exchange for a written guarantee that Blanche would rescind the $1.8 billion &quot;Anti-Weaponization Fund&quot; that allowed January 6 insurrectionists to claim payments from the federal government for their ensuing prosecution.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;In addition to written promises to cancel the January 6 fund, Blanche also agreed (in writing) that the provision exempting Trump and his family and businesses from audits would only apply to audits open at the time of the settlement.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately, now that Blanche&#39;s nomination has been confirmed, he is on his way to officially becoming the Attorney General, where he will undoubtedly serve as Trump&#39;s lapdog and continue to use the Department of Justice to target and punish Trump&#39;s political enemies with blatant disregard for the Constitution and rule of law.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/senate-blanche-trump-justice-fund-a38decfc7f20e4f73a181914d53111da&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(AP) GOP holdouts say they will back Blanche&#39;s attorney general nomination after striking deal over fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Jeanine Pirro admits Reflecting Pool damage was the result of shoddy construction &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/pirro-trump-reflecting-pool-damage-vandalism-fecb6e13f1475dfe8a38898360c0446f&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/paU7LzymCt-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Painting the Reflecting Pool blue&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/paU7LzymCt-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;533&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/paU7LzymCt-200.webp 200w, /images/paU7LzymCt-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Painting the Reflecting Pool blue.&lt;/b&gt; Image by &lt;a href=&quot;https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Lorax&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;G. Edward Johnson&lt;/a&gt; from &lt;a href=&quot;https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2026-05-15_Painting_the_Reflecting_Pool_Blue_Washington_DC_13-51-23_1.jpg&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Wikimedia Commons.&lt;/a&gt; Licensed under the &lt;a href=&quot;https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/deed.en&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Creative Commons Attribution-Share Alike 4.0 International license&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;For months now, Donny 2-Dolls has been pushing the false claim that the Reflecting Pool was damaged by vandals. U.S. Attorney for the District of Columbia Jeanine Pirro filed charges against David Hearn, a former Olympian, who was seen touching the damaged Reflecting Pool liner and later accused of damaging the national landmark. It was obvious to everyone who saw the problems with the Reflecting Pool that the damage was far too extensive and pervasive to be attributed to vandalism, but the Trump regime doubled down on its accusations, and Pirro publicly announced that Hearn was guilty before the trial.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Less than a month later, the U.S. Attorney&#39;s office was forced to drop the charges against Hearn, admitting they had no evidence of vandalism and that the damage to the Reflecting Pool was the result of shoddy installation that cost taxpayers more than $15 million and left the monument in worse shape than it was before Trump decided it needed to be &quot;fixed.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Naturally, Donny 2-Dolls is furious, claiming Pirro &quot;folded like an umbrella,&quot; and it is likely that Pirro will be fired. She won&#39;t be fired for filing false charges against an innocent man, but for backing down and admitting that there was not enough evidence to proceed with the blatantly unlawful case.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;July 2, 2026:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;blockquote&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;He damaged the pool...He reached down into the pool. Our evidence further shows that the National Park Service employees observed Hearn actually forcefully and violently pulling up and removing the bottom liner with both hands. According to witnesses, Hearn damaged approximately 2 square feet of sealant from the bottom of the pool.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;figcaption class=&quot;blockquote-footer&quot;&gt;Jeanine Pirro, U.S. Attorney&lt;/figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/blockquote&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;July 31, 2026&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;blockquote&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;It is difficult to attribute the widespread damage to the Reflecting Pool to vandalism, let alone to establish that fact beyond a reasonable doubt...&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;The damage was the result of a botched installation and not vandalism.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;figcaption class=&quot;blockquote-footer&quot;&gt;Jeanine Pirro, U.S. Attorney&lt;/figcaption&gt;
		&lt;/blockquote&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
