&lt;section class=&quot;block the-bad&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The bad...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        Trump regime&#39;s immigration crackdown detaining active duty servicemembers&#39; parents and spouses &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/military-families-immigration-trump-detained-deported-3337173bff1f06153738c217da52e846&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/8FLM68tj2j-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;Saying goodbye&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/8FLM68tj2j-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;533&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/8FLM68tj2j-200.webp 200w, /images/8FLM68tj2j-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;Image by &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com/users/foundry-923783/?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=864397&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Foundry Co&lt;/a&gt; from &lt;a href=&quot;https://pixabay.com//?utm_source=link-attribution&amp;utm_medium=referral&amp;utm_campaign=image&amp;utm_content=864397&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Pixabay&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;Dozens of family members of active-duty U.S. servicemembers have been detained by the Trump regime&#39;s goons as they attempt to carry out his mass deportation agenda. These detentions are the direct result of policy changes made by the regime to deliberately roll back protections traditionally offered to military families.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;For decades, families of military members have been protected from being deported until the Trump regime decided to withhold those protections, which have been strongly supported by both parties. Now, families of troops asked to put their lives on the line to defend the United States are being forcibly detained, often for months at a time, and many have been permanently deported. &lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;This is yet another example of the regime&#39;s complete and total disregard for the wellbeing of the country. Allowing this to happen to military families decreases our country&#39;s military readiness, dishonors the sacrifices of those who serve, and ensures that fewer people will volunteer to serve in our military in the future.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;blockquote&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;This administration just doesn’t care, and they are not thinking about people who are putting their lives on the line for the country and to defend our nation.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;figcaption class=&quot;blockquote-footer&quot;&gt;Representative Gil Cisneros, (D-CA)
		&lt;/blockquote&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/military-families-immigration-trump-detained-deported-3337173bff1f06153738c217da52e846&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(AP) Trump&#39;s immigration crackdown has detained more than 50 military spouses and parents&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;

&lt;section class=&quot;block the-ugly&quot;&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The ugly...&lt;/h4&gt;
	&lt;div class=&quot;blob&quot;&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-title&quot;&gt;
        ICE policy is to withhold body cam footage unless it shows agents in a favorable light &lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/ice-body-cameras-officers-shootings-dab1b294c8dc412d9ef8557ccbebfd57&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;[Link&lt;span class=&quot;bi bi-link-45deg&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;]&lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class=&quot;blob-content&quot;&gt;
        &lt;div class=&quot;image-right&quot; style=&quot;width:225px&quot;&gt;

    &lt;a href=&quot;/images/vWMQYDphUg-800.webp&quot; class=&quot;lightbox-link&quot; aria-haspopup=&quot;dialog&quot; style=&quot;cursor:zoom-in&quot;&gt;
      &lt;img class=&quot;img-lightbox&quot; alt=&quot;No ICE&quot; loading=&quot;lazy&quot; decoding=&quot;async&quot; style=&quot;--img-width:200&quot; src=&quot;/images/vWMQYDphUg-200.webp&quot; width=&quot;800&quot; height=&quot;600&quot; srcset=&quot;/images/vWMQYDphUg-200.webp 200w, /images/vWMQYDphUg-800.webp 800w&quot; sizes=&quot;200px&quot;&gt;
    &lt;/a&gt;

            &lt;p class=&quot;caption&quot;&gt;Image by &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.flickr.com/photos/11534965@N05/55069331551/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Dyan Bone&lt;/a&gt; from &lt;a href=&quot;https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ICE_out_for_Good!_January_23,_2026,_protest_in_Tucson,_Arizona_-_24.jpg&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Wikimedia Commons.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;In exchange for continued funding, ICE has recently been required to equip officers with body cameras. This requirement comes in response to multiple murders committed by ICE agents and the tendency of the agents and the department to lie about the circumstances surrounding those murders.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;The cameras, paid for by taxpayers, may be of limited use, considering that ICE&#39;s policy is to only release footage from these cameras if doing so is in the &quot;best interests of the agency.&quot; The decision on whether to release footage will be made solely at the discretion of the director of ICE, and the policy does not specify what circumstances warrant withholding the footage.&lt;/p&gt;
		&lt;p&gt;When Alex Pretti was murdered by CBP agents (A sister agency to ICE), his death was captured by body cameras worn by agents, but CBP has still not released footage of the killing. There is no reason to believe ICE would be any more forthcoming in sharing its own footage the next time its agents gun down an innocent person on the streets of the United States of America.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div&gt;
            &lt;div class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Related Links:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
            &lt;ul class=&quot;related-links&quot;&gt;
                &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://apnews.com/article/ice-body-cameras-officers-shootings-dab1b294c8dc412d9ef8557ccbebfd57&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;(AP) ICE will release body camera video only when seen in the agency&#39;s &quot;best interests,&quot; policy says&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
            &lt;/ul&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;/div&gt;
	&lt;hr style=&quot;clear:both&quot;/&gt;
&lt;/section&gt;


